                          VH - Hypertext Browser                         ========================  This is the GNU hypertext browser ported to OSK. It is compiled with mousesupport and can be fully enjoyed on an MM/1 with mouse, but it also should beusable on other OSK systems.  The screen.c file has been extensively modified to include mouse support andno effort was made to keep it similar to the original. The original sources canbe obtained from GNU sites, like prep.ai.mit.edu.The mouse functions are described in the nroff manual pages for vh. For yourconvenience I have included their PostScript translation.   Clicking the left button on a keyword moves us to the dictionary entry forthis keyword. Dragging the thumb (scroll box) on the scrollbar moves us acrossthe file. The middle button replaces the right button in the original and isused to backtrack. You can also click on the "help" or "exit" entries on thebottom line.  This port follows the original in using a text screen based on curses. A gra-phical screen would be more appropriate for MM/1.  The functionality of the program (described in full in the manual pages) in-cludes preparation of other hypertext input files (index generation), selectionof random entries (fortune cookies) and saving of the browsed entries for laterprinting.  The main program is called "jargon" rather than "vh" because it then directlysearches the file "jargon.txt" indexed by "jargon.idx" both from the directory/h0/vh (see below). To browse "example.txt" with the index "example.idx" type"jargon example".  To install the package, uncompress  it in the root directory (/h0). The mainprogram "jargon" will go to the CMDS directory and the rest to a newly createddirectory VH. Variable VHPATH in vh.c contains now the string "/h0/vh" - thename of the directory where the text and index files reside. This string mayconsist of several paths separated by colons.      Andrzej Kotanski (kotanski@zeus02.desy.de